From bd9e30b5da6852ee43a1a52701d3d952ccec6ad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:58:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 083/112] LPF: no analog noise on the ladders' cutoff any more
 (12 dB, 24 dB, drive): the rustle at low cutoff is gone

The 12 / 24 dB and drive ladders moved their stages' moveability by a heavily
lowpassed random value on every sample (about 0.44 % rms, below about 55 Hz,
from the global jcong generator). At low cutoff that was the audible rustle
(-21 to -42 dBc A-weighted). The stages now take the configured moveability
as it is; everything else is unchanged. The ladders no longer draw from jcong,
so other users of getNoise() get different (equally random) values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
